VS Code extension that live-previews Shattered Archive DSL color codes ({R, {G, {x, ...) in a side-by-side webview as the user types in any editor tab. Standalone package (not built with Vite/the app dev-server scripts like the other apps/* clients) — bundled with esbuild into a single dist/extension.js and either run via the Extension Development Host (F5) or packaged into a .vsix with vsce. The color renderer (src/renderDslToHtml.ts) is a deliberate hand-synced copy of game-client's renderDslColorPreviewHtml.ts, since a VSIX can't import across the workspace at runtime.
